### Recorded interpretations — ATT&CK descriptions are not treated as railway entailments

rssca:t0842-confidentiality-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0842-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow already assessed as confidentiality-vulnerable is a relevant target for the information-capture objective described by T0842." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK states that network sniffing captures traffic and specifically identifies information sent over unencrypted protocols. The L1 criterion supplies the separately sourced railway control assessment; this interpretation only maps its outcome to technique relevance."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t0814-rate-limiting-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0814-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow with the declared rate-limiting weakness is relevant to the request-volume manifestation of T0814." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK includes overwhelming a target with a high request volume as one T0814 manifestation. The mapping is deliberately narrower than the full technique and does not exclude vulnerability- or malformed-request-based denial of service."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t1692-001-authenticity-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t1692-001-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A safety-related flow with a derived critical authenticity violation is relevant to testing unauthorised command-message injection under T1692.001." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK ICS 19.2 replaces revoked T0855 with T1692.001 and defines the sub-technique as sending unauthorised command messages to control-system assets. The L2 outcome identifies a safety-related railway flow whose command authenticity warrants this test; it does not assert that a command was sent."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t0830-authentication-integrity-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0830-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow with both authentication and integrity weaknesses is relevant to the traffic-modification manifestation of T0830." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK states that established adversary-in-the-middle access can block, modify or inject traffic. Requiring both L1 weakness evaluations is a conservative railway test-planning policy and is not a claim that these weaknesses alone establish privileged network access."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t1691-001-timeliness-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t1691-001-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow with a critical timeliness violation is relevant to testing blocked command-message delivery under T1691.001." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK describes T1691.001 as blocking a command message from reaching its intended target and notes that blocked command messages can inhibit response functions. The L2 critical-timeliness criterion supplies the railway evidence that delayed emergency-command communication is safety-relevant; this mapping does not assert that blocking has occurred."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t1692-002-sequence-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t1692-002-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow with a critical sequence violation over position/status data is relevant to testing spoofed reporting messages under T1692.002." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK describes T1692.002 as spoofing reporting messages that contain telemetry data about the current state of equipment and the industrial process. The L2 critical-sequence criterion supplies the railway evidence that position/status sequence integrity is critical; this mapping does not infer that telemetry has been spoofed."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t0832-sequence-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0832-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow with a critical sequence violation over position/status data is relevant to testing manipulation of reported view under T0832." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK describes T0832 as manipulating information reported back to operators or controllers, so the process may be in a different state than reported. The L2 critical-sequence criterion supplies the railway evidence that a sequence-affected position/status flow is a critical reporting concern; this mapping does not assert operator deception or process manipulation."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t0830-critical-integrity-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0830-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow with a critical integrity violation is relevant to testing adversary-in-the-middle traffic modification under T0830." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK states that adversary-in-the-middle access can block, modify or inject traffic. The L2 critical-integrity criterion supplies the railway evidence that corruption of a safety-related payload is critical; this mapping does not assert that adversary-in-the-middle access exists."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t0831-authenticity-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0831-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow with a critical authenticity violation is relevant to testing manipulation of control under T0831." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK describes T0831 as manipulating physical process control and includes spoof command messages among its methods. The L2 critical-authenticity criterion supplies the railway evidence that masquerade-exposed safety-related communication is critical; this mapping does not assert that physical control was manipulated."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t0815-sequence-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0815-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow with a critical sequence violation over position/status data is relevant to testing temporary denial of reported view under T0815." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK describes T0815 as denying operator visibility by preventing status and reporting messages. The L2 critical-sequence criterion supplies the railway evidence that a position/status reporting flow is critical; this mapping does not assert that operator visibility has been denied."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t0829-sequence-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0829-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A flow with a critical sequence violation over position/status data is relevant to testing sustained loss of reported view under T0829." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK describes T0829 as sustained reporting or visibility loss that hides the present state of operations. The L2 critical-sequence criterion supplies the railway evidence that a position/status reporting flow is critical; this mapping does not assert that loss of view has occurred."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t0886-external-entry-point-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0886-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A railway asset already evaluated as an external-zone entry point is relevant to testing remote-service initial access or lateral movement under T0886." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK lists T0886 Remote Services under initial access and lateral movement. The L2 external-zone entry-point criterion supplies the railway-specific evidence that the asset is exposed as an entry point. This mapping does not assert credentials, service exploitability or attack occurrence."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .

rssca:t0886-dmz-entry-point-interpretation a rss-crit:Interpretation ;
    rss-crit:interprets rssca:t0886-location ;
    rss-crit:interpretationProposition "A railway asset already evaluated as a DMZ-zone entry point is relevant to testing remote-service initial access or lateral movement under T0886." ;
    rss-crit:reasoning "ATT&CK lists T0886 Remote Services under initial access and lateral movement. The L2 DMZ-zone entry-point criterion supplies the railway-specific evidence that the asset is reachable through the declared railway DMZ attack-surface policy. This mapping does not assert credentials, service exploitability or attack occurrence."@en ;
    rss-crit:interpretationConfidence "reasoned" ;
    rss-crit:reviewStatus "reviewed against ATT&CK ICS 19.2" .
